uman beings  and as members of society to have a bit  of a responsibility that even if the  stadium's two miles from us we're not  allowed to go so I wouldn't I would be  against playing in in your own stadium  but behind closed doors as they've done  in Germany so I don't think it's a  necessity for human I'm sorry for finito  stadiums but I do understand that if you  want to get back quicker you probably  will have to play behind closed doors  which isn't ideal  but nevertheless this is not an ideal  circumstance you know we have to make  them out of a bad situation so playing  in empty stadiums for me if we decide  that sooner rather than later we have to  get back to play I don't see that as a  problem and John just just been  obviously as a former you know Liverpool  player yourself I mean if Liverpool are  crowned champions you would expect to  see relegation happen as well what why  is that linkage necessary it's about the  integrity of the competition Liverpool  winning and not having promotion and  relegation I'm not a storm allegation  I'm talking about Leeds and West Brom  and crew in leak two or whatever coming  up you can't just arbitrarily  it's like saying well give leaves the  championship why just give Liverpool one  I'm going to leave the championship or  cruise they're top of league what it's  about honoring the competition it's not  just about Liverpool getting the  championship but forgetting everything  else it's about for me the integrity of  this of the competition not necessarily  just the score of the football but  competition that's why I'm perplexed to  find out why in Scotland they gave  Celtic the championship and relegated  hearts  but we just you know PFA is the trade  union of professional footballers how  worried are you that this this hiatus  when people who love football haven't  had access to it might might perhaps  teach some of them that they they can  live without it after all well I think  it's fair to say that we don't have 